[I] bash/POSIX-compatible shell implemented in Rust

[T] brush (Bo(u)rn(e) RUsty SHell) is a modern bash- and POSIX- compatible
[T] shell written in Rust. Run your existing scripts and .bashrc unchanged with
[T] syntax highlighting and auto-suggestions built in.

[U] https://github.com/reubeno/brush

[A] Reuben Olinsky
[M] foxdrodd

[C] extra/shell
[F] CROSS
[R] - alpha arc avr32 blackfin cris hppa hppa64 i860 m68k microblaze nios2 openrisc superh

[L] MIT
[V] 0.5.0

[D] 6784dc9a56b19bd9233bcab65c93765e61cbb62f3b4fee26ac96a62b brush-shell-0.5.0.tar.gz https://github.com/reubeno/brush/archive/brush-shell-v0.5.0/

cargoinstopt="${cargoinstopt/--path ./--path brush-shell} --bin brush"
